# Model checkpoints (large files).
# ⚠️ THIS IS A REPO-SIZE RULE AND IT HAS NO ISSUE BEHIND IT. Said here because the
# absence is what went wrong: with nothing to cite, ten documents cited #97 instead
# — and #97 is the TDM opt-out assessment, which is about ARTICLE TEXT and concluded
# the models are clean. Cite this section BY NAME -- line numbers move, and the
# line-number citation written when this note was added was stale the moment the
# note itself shifted them. Cite #97 only for article text and training splits,
# where it IS correct. (Corrected 2026-09-05.)
inference/models/*/
filters/**/model/
# probe pkls (e5-small, ~0.5MB) ARE committed — needed for hybrid inference + reproducibility.
# (removed blanket filters/**/probe/ ignore 2026-07-10). Large probe variants: ignore explicitly.
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pkl
# ...except filter hybrid-inference probes (small, needed, reproducible).
# NOTE: the comment must live on its own line — gitignore treats a trailing
# " # comment" as part of the pattern, which silently disabled this negation
# for months (probes were only tracked via per-directory .gitignore fixes).
!filters/*/v*/probe/*.pkl
# But track model metadata
!filters/**/training_*.json

# Datasets and data (large files - track metadata only)
datasets/*
datasets/*.jsonl
datasets/raw/
datasets/processed/
datasets/splits/
datasets/test/
data/

# Track metadata files for documentation
!datasets/*_metadata.json
!datasets/*/.*_metadata.json
!datasets/README.md

# Keep .gitkeep files for empty directories
!datasets/.gitkeep
!datasets/splits/.gitkeep
!inference/models/.gitkeep

# Calibration outputs (generated files)
calibrations/*/
reports/*.md
reports/*.json
reports/*.html
reports/*.docx
reports/*.pdf
reports/*/
!reports/README.md

# Experiment logs
experiments/*/
wandb/
logs/
*.log
*.log.*
calibration_run.log

# PyTorch/ML artifacts
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.tox/
test_batch_labeler.py
!tests/test_*.py

# Documentation builds
docs/_build/
site/

