notebooks/exploratory/
*.bak
*.old
*_backup.*
*_test.*

# ==============================================================================
# FreeFileSync - Large files handled by file sync, not git
# ==============================================================================
# These files are synced via FreeFileSync between local and GPU machine
# They should NOT be in git due to size

# Binary reports (keep locally, not in git)
*.docx

# Large model files (sync via FreeFileSync)
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.h5
*.keras

# Tokenizer files (download from HuggingFace, don't track in git)
**/model/tokenizer.json
**/model/vocab.json
**/model/merges.txt

# Large datasets
*.parquet
*.feather
*.arrow

# Checkpoints and training outputs
checkpoints/
training_outputs/
model_outputs/

# FreeFileSync backup and database files
.sync-backups/
*.ffs_db
*.ffs_lock

# Deployment artifacts
model_backup/
**/model_backup/
# ⛔ `README_MODEL.md` WAS IGNORED HERE UNTIL 2026-09-06, and the doc standard
# (memory/filter-doc-standard.md item 7) requires it in every filter package. Five
# existed on disk and NONE was tracked, so a fresh clone had no model card for any
# filter while every parity check counted the file as present. Its siblings are all
# derived-and-tracked — calibration.json, training_history.json, normalization.json
# — so being the one derived doc that is ignored was the inconsistency, not the rule.
# Regenerate with: upload_to_huggingface.py --filter <dir> --repo-name <id> --card-only

# Claude Code temp files
tmpclaude-*
*-cwd

# Reference PDFs: track the README pointer, keep binaries local
docs/references/*.pdf
filters/common/violence_promotion/training/*.jsonl

# Adverse examples are hand-curated evidence and ARE committed (datasets/adverse/README.md).
# Without these negations a new case is silently ignored by the datasets/ rule above.
!datasets/adverse/
!datasets/adverse/*.jsonl
# Candidates are UNADJUDICATED and must stay OUT of the datasets/adverse/*.jsonl
# glob that a future adverse-gate will read (docs/TODO.md, #91). Own subdir, own
# negation, so a glob cannot mistake a candidate for curated evidence.
!datasets/adverse/candidates/
!datasets/adverse/candidates/*.jsonl
!datasets/adverse/candidates/*.md

# Cross-box parity dumps ARE committed: they are the evidence behind a claim
# that a given box may or may not be used to measure at a given op-point
# (scripts/verification/box_parity.py). Small (~190 KB per 660-row split) and
# expensive to regenerate — ~30 min of CPU on the serving box, which can only be
# done between pipeline cycles. Without a negation the datasets/* rule above
# silently swallows them.
!datasets/parity/
!datasets/parity/*.jsonl
!datasets/parity/*.md

# Claude Code user-local settings — machine-specific permission list, never shared.
# Untracked 2026-08-06 (context audit): it had been committed and carried a
# different machine and user (C:/local_dev/..., C:/Users/scbry/...). The tracked
# .claude/skills/ reference installs stay tracked; only this file is local.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Evidence logs are the record behind a measured claim -- `*.log` above would drop
# them silently, and a docs/evidence/ page that references logs nobody else has is
# worse than no page. Negate for evidence only (2026-08-22).
!docs/evidence/**/*.log

# bash run sentinels written by background evidence runs — not evidence
docs/evidence/**/runs/*.status

# ⛔ THE SCRATCH RULES ABOVE (`*.bak`, `*.old`, `*_backup.*`, `*_test.*`) ARE PATTERNS,
# NOT PATHS, so they apply repo-wide. `*_test.*` silently swallowed a committed evidence
# artifact on 2026-09-04: `docs/evidence/2026-09-04-v8-probe-calibration/
# probe_recall_report_test.json` — the SOLE source for every test-split number published
# in that directory's README, in `filters/human_thriving/v8/calibration_report.md` and in
# EXP-016. `git add` omitted it without a word; its `_val` and `_test_seed7` siblings were
# staged, so the loss looked like nothing at all.
# Measured blast radius at the time (`git status --porcelain --ignored | grep '_test\.'`):
# two untracked files repo-wide — that JSON and
# `filters/common/obituary_detector/validation/panel_obit_test.py`.
# Evidence directories are the record a decision was made on; a scratch-file pattern must
# not be able to delete one.
!docs/evidence/**/*_test.*
!docs/evidence/**/*_backup.*
#
# ⛔ RECURRENCE 2026-09-05, AND THE FIRST FIX IS WHY. The 09-04 rescue above was scoped
# to `docs/evidence/` and its own note said so — "the pattern still swallows `*_test.*`
# anywhere else in the repo" — which made it a fix for the instance, not the defect.
# `scripts/gate/v8_smoke_test.py` was the third victim, ignored the moment it was
# written. ⭐ It surfaced only because `git add <explicit path>` WARNS; the 09-04 loss
# went silent because that was `git add <dir>`. Do not rely on the warning.
# SOURCE DIRECTORIES ARE NOW NEGATED TOO. A scratch-file pattern must never be able to
# swallow code or evidence; it exists for `notes_backup.md` in a working directory.
!scripts/**/*_test.*
!scripts/**/*_backup.*
!tests/**/*_test.*
!filters/**/*_test.*
!training/**/*_test.*
!ground_truth/**/*_test.*
# ⚠️ This also makes `filters/common/obituary_detector/validation/panel_obit_test.py`
# stageable — the second victim the 09-04 note named and nobody rescued. It is still
# untracked; committing it is a separate decision, not a side effect of this line.
